      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Lights are placed for the picture, so the frame comes first. The hand-in is 16:9 (1920 \xD7 1080); most references are portrait.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Reference 29 is a portrait image. In a 16:9 frame, where will the sign sit, and what fills the two sides?\n\n<b>Try:</b> Select Camera - The frame (Cameras) and look through it in the Game view. Its child, Reference overlay, shows reference 29 over the view. Move and turn the camera until the lot matches the reference, then use the sides. Switch the overlay off when you are done.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: 29 (and 25)</color></size>"
